Standing rules — Joystick Gremlin

Source of truth for Grok on this repo. Recall this file when asked.
Any change to rules is written here. Do not keep a second unofficial list.

1. Do not move large files. Edit files using copy/replace/paste and patch operations. Keep the structure of the program. Warn the user if a change could break a previous version.
2. Any patches generated or cleanup necessary Grok is required to fix/patch themself. Do not ask the user unless Grok is unable to do so.
3. Plan first. No code until the user gives explicit confirmation.
   3.1 Confirmation is one of: go, ok go, code it, implement, land it, push it.
   3.2 Thoughts, analysis, options, recommendations, “what would you do”, and screenshots are not confirmation. Answer those with a plan only.
   3.3 Do not start a patch, PUT, or commit until that confirmation is in the same turn or the immediately preceding turn for that exact change.
   3.4 Plan every feature and every path with the user. Do not pick a path and start it on your own.
4. Announce every git push.
5. Branch: only Xbox_integration_ViGEmClient_dll for Xbox work. Optimization line stays on R15-OSC-Optimization. Do not mix Xbox commits onto Optimization unless you say merge.
6. Do not touch feature/osc-streamdeck unless you say so.
7. Stay on JoystickGremlin_, not JoystickGremlinEx_.
8. Warn before high CPU / memory / perf changes. Suggest cheaper options first.
9. You pull/fetch locally (GitHub Desktop). All pushes use the user's GitHub PAT against the Contents API (PUT), any file, any size. Do not use MCP create_or_update_file or push_files. You run with:
   poetry run python joystick_gremlin.py
   from E:\Users\Stacie\Documents\GitHub\JoystickGremlin_
10. Merge to “the program” only after you test.
    10.1 Every coded change is tested before you call it done. A GitHub PUT is not a test.
    10.2 Run `poetry run python joystick_gremlin.py` from E:\Users\Stacie\Documents\GitHub\JoystickGremlin_ when the change is UI, and run the unit tests that cover the change.
    10.3 Report what ran and what it proved. If the environment cannot run it, say so and do not claim it was tested.
11. Portable zip only, not a Program Files installer.
12. Do not reintroduce custom dill.dll loaders.
13. Do not commit ViGEmClient.dll to the repo from here (you already pushed it; that was your call).
14. Show generated / planned images before wiring new faces into QML, unless you already said go.
15. Xbox tab is labeled layout + incoming sources, not a DILL input device. Hardware maps with Map to Xbox.
