20. EVO R hardware lock and measured JPEG inventory live in qml/vkb_evo_r_face_map.md. Read that file before changing hardware ids or measured JPEG centroids. Chip / hotspot / spine placement at runtime is qml/maps/vkb_evo_r.json. When a measured centroid changes, update the md row and the JSON node nx/ny in the same commit.
21. Face leaders — precision only. No guessing. No window-screenshot math.
    21.1 Root cause of missed leaders: (a) nx/ny were read off a GUI screenshot that includes gutters and chrome, but px/py are fractions of the painted JPEG only; (b) tag ends used mapToItem(_face) while photo ends used _stage.x, which is not face space. Do not repeat either.
    21.2 Measure on the source bitmap only. For EVO R that is qml/images/vkb_gladiator_rig.jpg (899 x 920). Pixel x,y of the control, then nx = x / width, ny = y / height.
    21.3 Prove the dots on a copy of that JPEG and show it in chat before changing QML. The user confirms the overlay, not a window screenshot.
    21.4 Write the confirmed row into qml/vkb_evo_r_face_map.md and the matching node nx/ny in qml/maps/vkb_evo_r.json in the same commit.
    21.5 Both ends of every leader must use the same item space:
         photoPt(nx, ny) = _img.mapToItem(_face, _ox + nx * _pw, _oy + ny * _ph)
         tagPt = item.mapToItem(_face, …)
         Never use _stage.x / _stage.y as face coordinates.
    21.6 If a dot is still off, change one pixel pair on the JPEG overlay, then one map row. Do not nudge from a window screenshot.
