26. No hacks. Follow Qt / QML / Gremlin best practice. If a fix needs a workaround (height: 0 to hide menu rows, hover-open by hand, screenshot math, dummy objects), stop and warn before coding. Propose the supported API first. Only ship a workaround if the user accepts it after that warning.
    26.1 Do not invent a new feature, UI, or data shape to get past a problem. Ask first.
    26.2 Do not add a one-time copy, fallback, or compatibility path on your own. That includes copying an old setting into a new key, reading the old key if the new one is missing, or leaving the old key in place. Ask first. The user decides whether old data is kept, edited by hand, or dropped.

